          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A basic fact in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            may be decomposed into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} p-adic integers
            for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            this says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spec%28Z%29"} Spec(Z)
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            by all its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disks"} formal disks
            and the complements of finitely many points, a fact that is crucial in the geometric interpretation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            and which motivates for instance the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} geometric Langlands correspondence
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#ArithmeticFractureSquares"} below
          %p
            Lifting this statement to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+arithmetic+geometry"}> higher arithmetic geometry
            ” the
            %em arithmetic fracture theorem
            says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
            (and suitably tame plain
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completion"} p-completion
            for all primes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+homotopy+theory"} p-adic homotopy theory
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#TheArithmeticFractureSquare"} below
          %p
            One finds that this arithmetic fracturing in stable homotopy theory is really a statement about the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+spectrum"} Moore spectrum
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            and that of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E,F
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+theories"} homology theories
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization
            at their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            decomposes into the separate Bousfield localizations. This generalized fracture theorem appears for instance in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
            for localization at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+K-theory"} Morava K-theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+E-theory"} Morava E-theory
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#GeneralFractureSquares"} below
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+theory"} cohesive homotopy theory
            every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            canonically sits in a fracture square formed from the localizations exhibited by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+cohesion"} infinitesimal cohesion
            this is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometric
            analog of the classical arithmetic fracture. (See
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#InCohesiveHomotopyTheory"} below
          %h2#Statement Statement
          %h3#ArithmeticFractureSquares In number theory and arithmetic geometry
          %p
            The statement in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            is the following:
          #ArithmeticFractureSquare.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
              of all the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} p-adic integers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi prime
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{p\;prime}{\prod} \mathbb{Z}_p
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              of the former, hence there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℚ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℚ
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi ℤ
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                                %mrow
                                  %mi p
                                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                  %mi prime
                              %msub
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mi p
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi prime
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{Q}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \nwarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Q}\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}}\left(\underset{p\;prime}{\prod} \mathbb{Z}_p \right) &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nwarrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \underset{p\;prime}{\prod} \mathbb{Z}_p
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Equivalently this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
              of the rationals with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+adeles"} integral adeles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Z}}
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+adeles"} ring of adeles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℚ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔸
                              %mi ℚ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔸
                              %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{Q}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \nwarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}} &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nwarrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Z}}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+adeles"} ring of adeles
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              of the integral adeles
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi ℚ
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℚ
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℤ
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathbb{Q} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Z}}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "category+of+monoids#PushoutOfCommutativeMonoids"} here
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              diagram in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
              (for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topology"} discrete topology
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Z}}
              with its profinite/
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion+of+a+ring"} completion
              topology).
          %p
            An original discussion is (
            %a{:href => "#Sullivan05"}> Sullivan 05, prop. 1.18
            ). Review includes (
            %a{:href => "#Riehl14"}> Riehl 14, lemma 14.4.2
            ).
          #GeometricMeaning.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
              we may think of
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{Z})
                  as an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+curve"} arithmetic curve
                  over
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1"} F1
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔸
                          %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Z}}
                  as the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+functions"} ring of functions
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disks"} formal disks
                  around all the points in this curve;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℚ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
                  as the ring of functions on the complement of a finite number of points in the curve;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔸
                          %mi ℚ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}
                  is the ring of functions on punctured formal disks around all points, at most finitely many of which do not extend to the unpunctured disk.
            %p
              Under this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analogy
              the arithmetic fracture square of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ArithmeticFractureSquare"}
              says that the curve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{Z})
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
              whose patches are the complement of the curve by some points, and the formal disks around these points.
            %p
              This kind of cover plays a central role in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %em>
                    %a{:href => "moduli+space+of+bundles#OverCurvesAndTheLanglandsCorrespondence"} Moduli stack of bundles over curves
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %em>
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} geometric Langlands correspondence
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %em>
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+conjecture+on+Tamagawa+numbers"} Weil conjecture on Tamagawa numbers
                  \.
          %h3#InHomotopyTheory In homotopy theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            the corresponding statement is that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            may be decomposed into that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+types"} rational homotopy types
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-complete+homotopy+types"} p-complete homotopy types
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-local+homotopy+types"} p-local homotopy types
          #FractureForSpectra.num_remark
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              satisfying at least one of the following sufficient conditions
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+space"} nilpotent space
                  with finitely generated
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-local+homotopy+type"} p-local homotopy type
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi ℚ
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi X
                          %mi p
                          %mo ∧
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi ℚ
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \simeq X_{\mathbb{Q}} \underset{(X_p^\wedge)_{\mathbb{Q}}}{\times} X_p^\wedge
            %p
              of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{\mathbb{Q}}
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completion"} p-completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_p^\wedge
              over the rationalization
              = succeed "of" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi X
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_p^\wedge)_{\mathbb{Q}}
              = succeed "-completions." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            This originates around (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldKan72"}> Bousfield-Kan 72, VI.8.1
            ). A detailed more modern account is in (
            %a{:href => "#MayPonto"}> May-Ponto, theorem 13.1.4
            ). A quick survey is in (
            %a{:href => "#Riehl14"}> Riehl 14, theorem 14.4.14
            ).
          %h3#InStableHomotopyTheory In stable homotopy theory
          %p
            Similar statements hold in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#TheArithmeticFractureSquare"} The arithmetic fracture square
          %p
            but more generally there are fracture squares for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            homology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \vee F
            whenever
            = succeed "-localization" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "-acyclic:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#GeneralFractureSquares"} General fracture squares
          %blockquote
            %p
              warning: a condition missing in the following, see the comment section of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/91057/381"} this MO reply
          %h4#TheArithmeticFractureSquare The arithmetic fracture square for spectra
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_p
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
                at the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+spectrum"} Moore spectrum
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \mathbb{F}_p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completion"} p-completion
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi p
                          %mo ∧
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_p^\wedge
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{\mathbb{Q}}
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
                at the
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+spectrum"} Moore spectrum
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi H
                        %mi ℚ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \mathbb{Q} \simeq H \mathbb{Q}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
          #SullivanArithmeticFracture.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Sullivan arithmetic square)
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the canonical square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi ℚ
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi ℚ
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                                %mi p
                              %msub
                                %mi L
                                %mi p
                              %mi X
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                              %mi p
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi p
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; L_{\mathbb{Q}}X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \nwarrow
                    \\\
                    L_{\mathbb{Q}}
                    \\left(
                    \\prod_p L_p X
                    \\right)
                    \&amp;&amp;  &amp;&amp;
                    X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nwarrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \prod_p L_p X
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
              (hence also a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
          %p
            Original statements of this include (
            %a{:href => "#Bousfield79"}> Bousfield 79
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Sullivan05"} Sullivan 05, prop. 3.20
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#VanKoughnett13"} van Koughnett 13, prop. 4.5
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Bauer11"} Bauer 11, lemma 2.1
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong (“one prime at a time”)
            %p
              The impact of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FractureForSpectra"}
              is that it decomposes the study of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"}> stable
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              into that of
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
                  and
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+homotopy+theory"} p-adic homotopy theory
                  for each prime
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %p
              Both the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{\mathbb{Q}}
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completion"} p-completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{p}^\wedge
              are typically much easier to analyze than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              itself and so the fracture theorem gives a way to decompose the remaining hard part of study of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              into that of
              = succeed "-local/" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              = succeed "-complete" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p More generally:
          #ReformulationOfProdOverPComletionByLocalizationAtCoproduct.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The product of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completions"} p-completions
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
              at the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi p
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee_p S \mathbb{F}_p
              of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+spectra"} Moore spectra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi p
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∨
                          %mi p
                        %mi S
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mi p
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\prod_p L_p X
                    \\simeq
                    L_{\vee_p S \mathbb{F}_p} X
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+equivalence"} Bousfield equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Bousf
                    %msub
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi p
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S (\mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}) \simeq_{Bousf} \vee_p S \mathbb{F}_p
                    \\,,
            %p and therefore also an equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi p
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\prod_p L_p X
                    \\simeq
                    L_{S (\mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z})} X
                    \\,.
          %p
            The first statement originates around (
            %a{:href => "Bousfield+localization+of+spectra#Bousfield79"}> Bousfield 79, prop. 2.6
            ), review includes (
            %a{:href => "Bousfield+localization+of+spectra#VanKoughnett13"}> van Koughnett 13, prop. 4.4
            ,
            = succeed ");" do
              %a{:href => "#Bauer11"} Bauer 11, below prop. 2.2
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/91057/381"} Strickland 12, MO comment
          #TwoThirdHexagon.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
              and at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+space"} localization of a space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-completion"} p-completion
              maps on spectra are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofibers"} homotopy cofibers
              of
              = succeed "-acyclifications" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_E(X) \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi S
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = S \mathbb{Q} \simeq H \mathbb{Q}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = S \mathbb{F}_p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+spectra"} Moore spectra
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              and of the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+field"} finite field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p = \mathbb{Z}/(p)
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "localization+of+a+space#Lurie"} Lurie 10, lecture 20
            %p
              Including this into the statement of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FractureForSpectra"}
              says that for spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              satisfying sufficient conditions as above, then the canonical diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
